    "result_text": "The full suite (the single acceptance test class plus its helpers) is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule for the `POST /api/owners` OfficeFloor pipeline. The tier is a derived field the `OwnerMapper` computes at response time, so \u2014 following the existing `namesakeCount` pattern \u2014 I persist the household size at creation and let the mapper read it.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **New pipeline step** \u2014 `AssignOwnerHouseholdSize.java`: a single-responsibility function that counts the household after the new owner is added (existing owners already assigned the same `householdId` by `AssignOwnerHousehold`, plus the new owner itself; 1 when it shares no household) and stores it via `owner.setHouseholdSize(...)`.\n\n2. **Wiring** \u2014 inserted the `assignHouseholdSize` step into `owners.POST.yml` right after `assignHousehold` (so `householdId` is already set) and before `save`.\n\n3. **Owner model** \u2014 added the `householdSize` field with its `household_size` column mapping and accessors.\n\n4. **OwnerMapper** \u2014 `membershipTier` now returns `GOLD` when `householdSize >= 3`, otherwise falls through to the unchanged SILVER/BRONZE logic. Kept the method small; no other logic added.\n\n5. **OpenAPI spec** \u2014 added `GOLD` to the `membershipTier` enum and updated the description (regenerates `OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum.GOLD`).\n\n6. **Schemas** \u2014 added `household_size INTEGER` to all four DB schema files (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres).\n\nThe new `coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` acceptance test passes, and the full suite is green.",
